## System Issues
- **Always search official sources (Apple support/developer docs, Homebrew docs, upstream docs) before doing anything system-related.** Never guesswork — fetch first.
- This applies to ALL phases: installation, configuration, AND troubleshooting. If something is not working, fetch the official docs for that tool before attempting any fix. Never rely on training data to diagnose or fix system issues.
- macOS ships BSD userland tools (`sed`, `grep`, `stat`, etc.), not GNU — check flags before using them.
- Never randomly delete or add packages — verify what's installed first (`brew list`, `brew uses --installed`), check dependencies, confirm with user before removing anything.
- Prefer well-maintained, reliable packages over obscure or outdated ones.
- When upgrading or replacing something, always ask the user if they want to remove/clean up the old one before proceeding.
- Background services installed via Homebrew are managed with `brew services`, never with `sudo` unless the docs require it.
