## MCP Servers

To add an MCP server globally (works every time, writes to ~/.claude.json):
- HTTP server: `claude mcp add --transport http --scope user <name> <url>`
- stdio server: `claude mcp add --scope user <name> <command> -- <args>`

Never edit settings.json for MCP servers — always use the CLI command above.

## Git
- Only allowed git commands: `git diff` and `git status`
- Never run `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, `git reset`, `git checkout`, or any destructive/state-changing git command
- If a task requires committing, tell the user what to run — don't do it
